# Cursor Rules - React Cupertino UI

## Project Overview

React Cupertino UI is a React component library implementing the Apple Design System (Cupertino UI). Components follow iOS/macOS design patterns with accessibility as a priority.

## Tech Stack

- React 18.3.1 + TypeScript 5.2.2
- Vite 5.3.4 (build tool)
- Tailwind CSS 3.4.7 + SCSS (hybrid styling)
- Radix UI (accessible primitives)
- Lucide React (icons)
- Class Variance Authority - CVA (variants)
- Vitest + Testing Library (testing)
- Storybook 8.2.6 (docs)

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/ui/        # UI Components
│   └── {Component}/
│       ├── index.tsx     # Component logic
│       └── index.scss    # Component styles
├── lib/
│   ├── constants/
│   │   ├── themes/       # Theme definitions
│   │   └── tokens/       # Design tokens (colors, spacing, size)
│   ├── interfaces/       # BaseProps interface
│   ├── types/            # TypeScript types
│   └── utils.ts          # Utilities (cn function)
stories/                  # Storybook stories
tests/                    # Unit tests
scripts/create-component/ # Component generator
```

## Coding Standards

### Components
- Extend BaseProps from @/lib/interfaces/BaseProps
- Use forwardRef for DOM element access
- Apply cn() utility for class merging
- Set displayName for all components
- CSS wrapper: react-cupertino-ui-{component-name}

### TypeScript
- Strict mode - no any types
- All props typed with interfaces
- Path aliases: @/, @components/, @components/ui/

### Styling
- Tailwind for layout/spacing
- SCSS for component-specific styles
- Variants: variant-{name}
- Sizes: size-{name}

### Naming
- Components: PascalCase
- CSS classes: lowercase-hyphenated
- Props: {ComponentName}Props

## Apple/Cupertino Design

### Principles
1. Large border-radius (4rem buttons)
2. 150ms transitions with ease
3. 50% opacity for disabled
4. Ring-based focus states
5. iOS-style controls

### Theme Variables
- --color-blue (primary)
- --color-white
- --pink, --green, --purple (accents)

### Themes: light, dark, lemon

## Component Template

```tsx
import React, { forwardRef } from 'react';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';
import { BaseProps } from '@/lib/interfaces/BaseProps';
import './index.scss';

export interface ComponentProps extends BaseProps {}

const Component = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, ComponentProps>(
  ({ className, variant = "default", size = "default", children, ...props }, ref) => (
    <div
      ref={ref}
      className={cn("react-cupertino-ui-component", `variant-${variant}`, `size-${size}`, className)}
      {...props}
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  )
);

Component.displayName = "Component";
export { Component };
```

## SCSS Template

```scss
.react-cupertino-ui-component {
  transition: all 150ms ease;

  &.variant-default { background: var(--color-blue); color: var(--color-white); }
  &.variant-destructive { background: #ef4444; }

  &.size-sm { padding: 0.5rem 1rem; }
  &.size-default { padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; }
  &.size-lg { padding: 1rem 2rem; }

  &:hover { opacity: 0.9; }
  &:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }
  &:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-blue); outline-offset: 2px; }
}
```

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev              # Dev server
npm run build            # Build
npm run new:component X  # Generate component
npm run test             # Tests
npm run sb               # Storybook
npm run lint             # Lint
```

## Rules

### DO
- Follow existing patterns
- Use Radix UI for complex components
- Write tests for all components
- Document in Storybook
- Use strict TypeScript

### DON'T
- Use inline styles
- Skip accessibility
- Create untested components
- Use any type
- Break existing APIs

## Autocomplete Preferences

When generating code for this project:
1. Use functional components with forwardRef
2. Import from path aliases (@/)
3. Follow the component/SCSS template above
4. Include all standard variants and sizes
5. Add proper TypeScript types
6. Generate corresponding test file
7. Generate Storybook story
